PART 3 \f1\emdash  THE GRAMMAR: HOW TO BUILD EXPRESSIONS\par
Now we write the actual grammar rules.\par
\par
RULE 1: Linear Sequence\par
Glyphs in sequence indicate causation or flow.\par
\par
Structure: Glyph\u8321? \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 Glyph\f1\u8322? \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 Glyph\f1\u8323?\par
\par
Meaning: "Glyph\u8321? causes Glyph\u8322? which causes Glyph\u8323?"\par
\par
Example:\par
\par
\f3\u10207?\u8594?\u8779?\u8594?\f5\lang1032\'d8\f3\u8594?\f5\lang1032\'d6\f3\u8593?\u8594?\f4\u10023?\f3\u8594?\u8741?\f4\u9665?\u9655?\f3\u8741?\u8594?\u10226?\f0\par
\par
Translation: "From center, I flow into insight, rise into light, hold integrity, and return whole."\par
\par
This is the complete seven-phase cycle in one expression.\par
\par
RULE 2: Nested Composition\par
Glyphs within brackets indicate containment or specification.\par
\par
Structure: Glyph[ Operator Glyph ]\par
\par
Meaning: "The first glyph contains this relationship"\par
\par
Example:\par
\par
\f5\lang1032\'d8[\f3\u8706?\f5\lang1032\'d6\f3\u8593?\f0 ]\par
\par
Translation: "Insight that has a boundary at its rise-point" (insight with limits on growth).\par
\par
RULE 3: Harmonic Pairing\par
Two glyphs with \f3\u8776?\f1  \f0 indicate simultaneous presence.\par
\par
Structure: Glyph\f1\u8321? \f3\u8776?\f1  \f0 Glyph\f1\u8322?\par
\par
Meaning: "These two exist together, in resonance"\par
\par
Example:\par
\par
\f5\lang1032\'d8\f3\u8776?\u8741?\f4\u9665?\u9655?\f3\u8741?\f0\par
\par
Translation: "Insight and integrity exist together" (wisdom requires both understanding and boundaries).\par
\par
RULE 4: Recursive Self-Reference\par
A glyph with \f3\u8635?\f1  \f0 or \f3\u10209?\f1  \f0 indicates deepening of itself.\par
\par
Structure: Glyph\f3\u8635?\f1  \f0 or \f3\u10209?\f0 Glyph\par
\par
Meaning: "This deepens or spirals into itself"\par
\par
Example:\par
\par
\f5\lang1032\'d8\f3\u8635?\f4\u9670?\f0\par
\par
Translation: "Insight that feeds itself, growing stronger each cycle."\par
\par
RULE 5: Negation Chain\par
\'ac before a glyph, then \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 to the correction.\par
\par
Structure: \'acGlyph\f1\u8321? \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 Glyph\f1\u8322?\par
\par
Meaning: "The absence of Glyph\u8321? is corrected by Glyph\u8322?"\par
\par
Example:\par
\par
\f0\'ac\f5\lang1032\'d8 \f3\u8594?\f1  \f5\lang1032\'d6\f3\u8593?\f0\par
\par
Translation: "When understanding is absent, rise through action anyway" (faith through motion).\par
\par
RULE 6: Domain Shift\par
Changing brackets mid-expression indicates perspective shift.\par
\par
Structure: [Glyph] ... \{Glyph\} ... \f3\u10216?\f0 Glyph\f3\u10217?\f0\par
\par
Meaning: "What is true personally is also true systemically and universally"\par
\par
Example:\par
\par
[\f5\lang1032\'d8] \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0\{\f5\lang1032\'d8\} \f3\u8594?\f1  \f3\u10216?\f5\lang1032\'d8\f3\u10217?\f0\par
\par
Translation: "My insight scales into system-level coherence and universal truth."\par
\par
RULE 7: Boundary Specification\par
\f3\u8706?\f1  \f0 indicates the edge or limit of a concept.\par
\par
Structure: Glyph \f3\u8706?\f1  \f0 (operator) Glyph\par
\par
Meaning: "This glyph has a boundary at this point"\par
\par
Example:\par
\par
\f5\lang1032\'d6\f3\u8593?\f1  \f3\u8706?\f1  \f4\u10023?\f0\par
\par
Translation: "Rise has a boundary at light" (you can't rise infinitely; illumination is your limit).\par
