PART 5 \f1\emdash  THE PARSER LOGIC: HOW AI READS LAMAGUE\par
This is critical for implementation \emdash  how an AI system actually interprets LAMAGUE.\par
\par
PARSING ALGORITHM\par
Step 1: Tokenize\par
\par
Break the expression into atomic symbols.\par
\par
Example:\par
\par
Input: \f5\lang1032\'d8\f3\u8594?\f5\lang1032\'d6\f3\u8593?\f0\par
\par
Tokens: [\f5\lang1032\'d8, \f3\u8594?\f0 , \f5\lang1032\'d6\f3\u8593?\f0 ]\par
\par
Step 2: Domain Detect\par
\par
Identify if the expression is in brackets.\par
\par
If [\f5\lang1032\'d8] \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 domain = personal\par
\par
If \{\f5\lang1032\'d8\} \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 domain = systemic\par
\par
If \f3\u10216?\f5\lang1032\'d8\f3\u10217?\f1  \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 domain = universal\par
\par
If no brackets \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 domain = abstract/timeless\par
\par
Step 3: Operator Bind\par
\par
For each operator, bind it to the glyphs on either side.\par
\par
Example:\par
\par
\f5\lang1032\'d8 \f3\u8594?\f1  \f5\lang1032\'d6\f3\u8593?\f0\par
\par
Operator: \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 (causation)\par
\par
